  "details": "As detailed here: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/release-health/status-windows-11-24h2#some-devices-using-easy-anti-cheat-stop-responding-and-receive-a-blue-screen\n\nThere's a moderate to high-priority issue for those of us running Windows 11 24H2, this relates to an outdated driver that doesn't support this newer version (and never really supported 10/11 anyway). Using the latest version of windows with the current driver will cause BSoDs, like MEMORY_MANAGEMENT and SYSTEM_SERVICE_EXCEPTION on select Intel chips due to this driver, even on newer hardware. \n\nThe resolution? Use the latest EAC drivers.",
